{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetricSeparation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetricSeparation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_eq_zero_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_eq_zero_eq","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetricSeparation.lean#L318-L326","doc":"**Full separation — `dH` is a certified metric.**  `dH x y = 0 → x = y`,\ncombining every coordinate via `dH_eq_zero_coord` (which covers the height\ncoordinate too — the vertical FTC bound is the special case `i = 2`).  Together\nwith `dH_self`, `dH_comm`, `dH_triangle`, and `dH_nonneg` (all on `HyperbolicMetric`)\nthis is the full `ℝ≥0∞`-valued metric axiom set for `dH`, DERIVED — unconditional,\nindependent of the `HypMinimizerUnique` conjecture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_eq_zero_coord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.dH_eq_zero_coord","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetricSeparation.lean#L263-L316","doc":"**Horizontal separation (bean `qou-v8u3`).**  `dH x y = 0` forces every\ncoordinate of `x` and `y` to agree.  For the height coordinate this is\n`dH_eq_zero_height`; here we run the calculus-of-variations bound on coordinate\n`i`: for every admissible `γ`, `|y i − x i| ≤ (x₂ e^L)·L`, and `dH x y = 0` lets\n`L → 0`, so `|y i − x i| = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.majorant_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.majorant_le","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetricSeparation.lean#L255-L261","doc":"For `r ∈ [0,1]` and `A > 0`: `A · e^r · r ≤ A · e · r`.  (Monotone majorant used\nin the limit.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.horizDisplacement_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.horizDisplacement_le","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetricSeparation.lean#L193-L251","doc":"**Horizontal displacement bound.**  On a finite-length admissible path, for any\ncoordinate `i`, `|y i − x i| ≤ (x₂ · e^L) · L` with `L = realLen γ`.  The height\nceiling `height_le` dominates the coordinate derivative by `(x₂ e^L)·g`, and the\nFTC on coordinate `i` turns the displacement into `∫ (γ' )i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.height_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.height_le","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetricSeparation.lean#L111-L189","doc":"**Height ceiling (upper companion of `dH_ge_logHeight`).**  On a finite-length\nadmissible path, the height stays below `x₂ · e^L`: `(γ s)₂ ≤ (x)₂ · exp (realLen γ)`\nfor every `s ∈ [0,1]`.  Proof: FTC on `[0,s]` for `log∘z` gives\n`log z(s) − log z(0) = ∫₀ˢ z'/z ≤ ∫₀ˢ ‖γ'‖/z ≤ ∫₀¹ g = L`, then exponentiate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.realLen_eq_integral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.realLen_eq_integral","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetricSeparation.lean#L94-L107","doc":"**`realLen γ = ∫_{Ioc 0 1} g`** — the real length is the Bochner integral of the\nspeed (the `ofReal`↔`lintegral` bridge). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.integral_speedFn_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.integral_speedFn_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetricSeparation.lean#L88-L92","doc":"`∫_{Ioc 0 1} g ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.speedFn_integrableOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.speedFn_integrableOn","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetricSeparation.lean#L76-L86","doc":"On a finite-length admissible path, the speed integrand is integrable on\n`Icc 0 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.speedFn_aesm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.speedFn_aesm","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetricSeparation.lean#L63-L74","doc":"The speed integrand is a.e.-strongly-measurable on `Icc 0 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.speedFn_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.speedFn_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetricSeparation.lean#L59-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.speedFn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.speedFn","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetricSeparation.lean#L56-L57","doc":"The speed integrand `g t = ‖γ' t‖ / (γ t)₂` whose lintegral is `pathLenH`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.realLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric.realLen","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicMetricSeparation.lean#L53-L54","doc":"The **real hyperbolic length** of a path: `(pathLenH γ).toReal`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}